IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `it-types`
IMPORT `it-liability`

-- Income Tax Act 2007, personal income tax — GOAL 3: CREDITS, TERMINAL TAX
-- AND REFUNDS.
--
--   "What is the person's independent earner tax credit; and once their
--    credits are used, what terminal tax do they owe or what refund are
--    they due?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2007_97.txt — ss BC 8,
-- LA 2-LA 7, LC 13-LC 15.

§ `Goal 3 — credits, terminal tax and refunds`

§§ `The independent earner tax credit (ss LC 13-LC 15)`

-- LC 13 "(1) This section applies for a natural person, for a period (the
-- credit period) in a tax year when the person— (a) is not receiving a main
-- benefit; and (b) ... a veteran's pension; and (c) ... New Zealand
-- superannuation; and (d) is not entitled to or is not receiving a WFF tax
-- credit; and (e) is not the spouse ... of a person who is entitled to and is
-- receiving a WFF tax credit; and (f) [no overseas equivalent]; and (g) [no
-- partner's overseas WFF equivalent]; and (h) is resident in New Zealand."
@ref s LC 13(1)
GIVEN f IS AN `Independent earner facts`, resident IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section LC 13 applies to` f `, resident` resident IF
        NOT f's `receiving a main benefit, veteran's pension or New Zealand superannuation`
    AND NOT f's `entitled to or receiving a WFF tax credit, or the partner of someone receiving one`
    AND NOT f's `receiving an overseas equivalent, or the partner of someone receiving an overseas WFF equivalent`
    AND resident

-- LC 13 "(4) Person's credit is, if the person's net income for the tax year
-- is equal to or more than $24,000, $520. Otherwise it is zero. (5) Full year
-- abatement is, if the person's net income is greater than $66,000 for the
-- tax year, 13 cents for each complete dollar of the excess." LC 14(5) uses
-- $44,000.
@ref s LC 13(4)-(5), LC 14(5)
GIVEN net IS A NUMBER, threshold IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the person's credit less the full year abatement, net income` net `, abatement above` threshold MEANS
    credit MINUS abatement
    WHERE
        credit MEANS IF net AT LEAST 24000 THEN 520 ELSE 0
        abatement MEANS IF net GREATER THAN threshold THEN 0.13 TIMES FLOOR (net MINUS threshold) ELSE 0

-- LC 13 "(2) For the credit period, the person has a tax credit equal to the
-- positive amount calculated using the formula" (lost in the conversion; its
-- items are the person's credit, the full year abatement and the credit
-- period months): read as (credit − abatement) × months ÷ 12 (fork F2).
-- LC 14 and LC 15 split the 2024-25 tax year at 31 July 2024 and count
-- credit period days: read as ÷ 365, the days in that tax year (fork F2).
-- The text as at 2026 gives no rule for a tax year before 2024-25.
@ref ss LC 13-LC 15
@export The independent earner tax credit for a natural person under ss LC 13-LC 15 of the Income Tax Act 2007 (NZ): for a New Zealand resident with no main benefit, veteran's pension, New Zealand superannuation or Working for Families tax credit (or overseas equivalent), $520 if net income is $24,000 or more, less 13 cents for each complete dollar over $66,000, pro rata to the whole months of the credit period (for 2024-25, $44,000 until 30 July 2024, by days). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS AN `Independent earner facts`  @desc Benefits, pensions, superannuation and Working for Families (or overseas equivalents), and the length of the credit period
      net IS A NUMBER  @desc The person's net income for the tax year
      year IS A NUMBER  @desc The tax year, by the 31 March it ends on
      resident IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the person is resident in New Zealand
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the independent earner tax credit for` f `, net income` net `, tax year ending` year `, resident` resident MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `section LC 13 applies to` f `, resident` resident THEN 0
        IF year LESS THAN 2025 THEN `the text as at 2026 gives no independent earner rule before 2024-25`
        IF year EQUALS 2025 THEN
                max 0 (`the person's credit less the full year abatement, net income` net `, abatement above` 44000 TIMES f's `whole days in the credit period to 30 July 2024` DIVIDED BY 365)
            PLUS max 0 (`the person's credit less the full year abatement, net income` net `, abatement above` 66000 TIMES f's `whole days in the credit period from 31 July 2024` DIVIDED BY 365)
        OTHERWISE max 0 (`the person's credit less the full year abatement, net income` net `, abatement above` 66000 TIMES f's `whole months in the credit period` DIVIDED BY 12)

`the text as at 2026 gives no independent earner rule before 2024-25` MEANS
    REFUSE "the version of ss LC 13-LC 15 as at 4 September 2026 gives no rule for a tax year before 2024-25"

§§ `Using credits (ss BC 8, LA 2-LA 7)`

DECLARE `Credit outcome` HAS
    `terminal tax`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `refund due`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `non-refundable credit extinguished`                IS A NUMBER
    `supplementary dividend credit remaining`           IS A NUMBER
    `imputation credit remaining`                       IS A NUMBER

-- LA 4 "(1) If a person's total tax credit ... is greater than their income
-- tax liability ..., the person must use their total tax credit ... by
-- using— (a) first, a non-refundable tax credit: (b) second, a tax credit for
-- a supplementary dividend: (c) third, a tax credit for an imputation credit:
-- [(d)-(e) R&D credits, not in scope]: (f) sixth, a refundable tax credit."
-- LA 3 / BC 8(3): if the credits are less, "the difference is the person's
-- terminal tax". LA 5 "(2) A non-refundable tax credit is extinguished ...
-- (3) [supplementary dividend credits are used under LP 3] (4) [imputation
-- credits under LE 2-LE 3] ... (6) The Commissioner refunds a refundable tax
-- credit by applying section LA 6, LA 7, or LA 8." Refunds are shown before
-- any LA 6(2) set-off against other years. LD 1(5): a donation credit "is
-- excluded from the application of sections LA 2 to LA 6", so it does not
-- satisfy the liability and is refunded whole (added after the independent
-- pass).
@ref ss BC 8, LA 2-LA 7
@export How a natural person's tax credits satisfy their income tax liability under ss BC 8 and LA 2-LA 7 of the Income Tax Act 2007 (NZ): used in order — non-refundable credits (including the independent earner tax credit), supplementary dividend credits, imputation credits, then refundable credits; any shortfall is terminal tax; remaining non-refundable credits are extinguished, and remaining refundable credits are refunded (before any set-off against other years), with donation credits (s LD 1) refunded whole rather than used against the liability. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN liability IS A NUMBER  @desc The income tax liability for the year
      c IS A Credits  @desc The person's other non-refundable, supplementary dividend, imputation and refundable credits
      ietc IS A NUMBER  @desc The independent earner tax credit
GIVETH A `Credit outcome`
`the use of credits against` liability `, credits` c `, independent earner tax credit` ietc MEANS
    `Credit outcome` WITH
        `terminal tax`                                  IS max 0 (liability MINUS (nonRefundable PLUS supp PLUS imputation PLUS refundable))
        `refund due`                                    IS max 0 (refundable MINUS left3) PLUS c's `donation tax credits under LD 1`
        `non-refundable credit extinguished`            IS max 0 (nonRefundable MINUS liability)
        `supplementary dividend credit remaining`       IS max 0 (supp MINUS left1)
        `imputation credit remaining`                   IS max 0 (imputation MINUS left2)
    WHERE
        nonRefundable MEANS c's `other non-refundable tax credits` PLUS ietc
        supp MEANS c's `supplementary dividend tax credits`
        imputation MEANS c's `imputation credits`
        refundable MEANS c's `refundable tax credits under LA 6` PLUS c's `refundable tax credits under LA 7`
        left1 MEANS max 0 (liability MINUS nonRefundable)
        left2 MEANS max 0 (left1 MINUS supp)
        left3 MEANS max 0 (left2 MINUS imputation)
